(EXP-90: the zero-pad format specifier converts a number to padded text -
 the manual's `{h:02}` on 9 gives "09".
 The extra lines record that the width is a minimum rather than a truncation:
 a number already wider than the field is not cut down.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-90.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   09
   005
   2026
)
a number called h is 9.
a text called hpadded is "{h:02}".
Print the hpadded.
a number called tick is 5.
Print "{tick:03}".
a number called census is 2026.
Print "{census:02}".
